[medium] Both `fileExistsFunction` and `fileEmptyFunction` are registered without any null check. Even though they're `@Singleton`, this presumes the beans are always injected and that `Extension` is always created via DI. To stay consistent with `render*` and `errorLogs`, either fail fast with a clear message when injection somehow yields null (for example, `Objects.requireNonNull(fileExistsFunction, "...")`), or mark them `@Nullable` and register them only when present. Otherwise, a wiring or classpath change in some distributions turns into an NPE during template engine initialization that is hard to diagnose.

```suggestion
        functions.put("randomInt", new RandomIntFunction());
        functions.put("randomPort", new RandomPortFunction());
        functions.put("fileExists", java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(fileExistsFunction, "fileExistsFunction bean is missing"));
        functions.put("fileEmpty", java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(fileEmptyFunction, "fileEmptyFunction bean is missing"));
```
